1. Hospital Management System – Core Answer
AnswerFunctional users: Patients register/login, book appointments, view medical history, download reports and reset passwords. Doctors view records, approve/change appointments, issue prescriptions and update reports. Admins manage schedules, monitor the system and generate reports. Key non-functional requirements: security, usability and smooth operation under high concurrent load.
2. Maven / Eclipse – HMS
a) Clone/import HMS.git clone https://github.com/ssvkotamraju/HMS.git
cd HMS
mvn -v
# Eclipse: File -> Import -> Maven -> Existing Maven Projects -> select HMS -> Finish.


b) 'mvn' is not recognized.Reason: Maven is not installed or Maven's bin directory is not in PATH.
1. Install Maven.
2. Set MAVEN_HOME to the Maven folder.
3. Add %MAVEN_HOME%\bin to PATH.
4. Open a new terminal and run:
mvn -v


c) Dependency resolution errors.Run:
mvn dependency:tree
mvn -U clean install
Check the exact groupId/artifactId/version in pom.xml, repository/network errors, and Java version.
In Eclipse: right-click project -> Maven -> Update Project -> Force Update.
Correct invalid coordinates/versions or add the required repository only when necessary.

d) Compilation failure.Run:
mvn clean install
Read the FIRST compiler error, note file and line number, inspect the related source/dependency, then fix it.
Run again with:
mvn clean install -e
# For full diagnostics:
mvn clean install -X

e) Java-version mismatch.mvn -v
java -version
Check pom.xml compiler source/target.
Set them to the installed JDK, for example:
<properties>
  <maven.compiler.source>8</maven.compiler.source>
  <maven.compiler.target>8</maven.compiler.target>
</properties>
Then set Eclipse Project JRE to the same JDK and run:
mvn clean install

f) Temporarily skip tests.mvn clean package -DskipTests
# Or skip test compilation and execution:
mvn clean package -Dmaven.test.skip=true
Risk: broken tests may hide defects; do this only temporarily and run the tests later.

g) Resolve dependency conflict.mvn dependency:tree
Find the library appearing with multiple versions. Prefer one compatible version by declaring it directly in pom.xml, or exclude the unwanted transitive dependency:
<exclusions>
  <exclusion>
    <groupId>...</groupId>
    <artifactId>...</artifactId>
  </exclusion>
</exclusions>
Then run mvn clean install.


h) Troubleshoot unexpected behavior after pom.xml change.git diff pom.xml
mvn dependency:tree
mvn help:effective-pom
mvn clean package
Compare old/new dependency versions, scopes and exclusions. Revert the POM change if it is the cause.
i) BUILD SUCCESS but browser fails.Check:
1. Server/container is actually running.
2. Correct port and context path.
3. WAR is present in target/ and deployed.
4. Server logs for startup/deployment errors.
5. Browser URL and application mappings.
6. Port 8080 is free/in use.
Use:
mvn tomcat7:run

# or the configured server in Eclipse.
j) Build plugin cannot be found/executed.Inspect pom.xml:
- <build>
- <plugins>
- <pluginManagement>
- plugin <groupId>, <artifactId>, <version>
- plugin configuration/goals
Also check Maven/JDK version and repository/network settings before changing source code.


