4. Docker – HMS
Initial Docker commands.# Dockerfile
FROM openjdk:17-jdk-slim
WORKDIR /app
COPY target/HMS.jar app.jar
EXPOSE 8080
ENTRYPOINT ["java","-jar","app.jar"]

docker build -t HMS .
docker run -d --name hms-container -p 8080:8080 HMS

a) Consistent environment.Docker packages the application with a fixed runtime, libraries, configuration and startup command. The same image can be run by all developers, avoiding differences in Java/server setup.

b) Important Dockerfile instructions.FROM, WORKDIR, COPY/ADD, RUN, ENV when needed, EXPOSE, and ENTRYPOINT/CMD. For a Java application, COPY the built JAR/WAR and define the command that starts it.

c) docker build fails.docker build -t HMS .

Check the FIRST error in the build output, verify Dockerfile syntax, file names/paths, build context, base image availability and permissions. Rebuild after correction.
d) Container port 8080 not reachable.docker run -d --name hms-container -p 8080:8080 HMS
# Verify:
docker ps
docker logs hms-container
# Host 8080 -> container 8080.

e) Tag and push to Docker Hub.docker tag HMS <dockerhub-username>/HMS:v1
docker login
docker push <dockerhub-username>/HMS:v1
